                                "sense_id": "b7ab55a4-b597-3f3d-92c5-8cde9febb463",
                                "text": "A heavily laurelled Irish bard – no, not the one you're thinking of: another one, with less talent – was reading a purportedly humorous poem to the usual sporadic titters, and I heard a recognizable Scots voice in the crowd near me growl, 'I don't think that's funny. Why does anyone think that's funny. I don't think that's funny.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3430879a-6d3a-42fa-aba8-e19084761f07",
                                "sense_id": "b7ab55a4-b597-3f3d-92c5-8cde9febb463",
                                "text": "Her most laurelled novels, which make up The Wonderland Quartet, include the National Book Award–winning Them, and charts the decline of working-class America in the 1960s."
                            }
                        ]
